This directory contains the Eclipse plugin (OSGi bundle) that integrates OpenJML
into the Eclipse IDE using the LSP interface to Eclipse.

The plugin acts as an LSP client, connecting to the OpenJML LSP server
(openjml-lsp from the OpenJMLlsp directory). It uses LSP4E to manage the
connection and LSP4J for the LSP protocol. Syntax highlighting is provided
via TM4E using the TextMate grammars in syntaxes/.

Key source files (src/):
  org.openjml.ui.Activator                     -- Plugin lifecycle, early startup handler
  org.jmlspecs.openjml.eclipse/
    OpenJMLPreferences.java                    -- Eclipse preferences page for OpenJML settings
    OpenJMLStreamConnectionProvider.java       -- LSP connection provider (launches openjml-lsp)
    LspPartListener.java                       -- Detects editor opens, connects documents to LSP
    JmlFoldingManager.java                     -- Code folding for JML annotations
    JmlNature.java / JmlNatureHandler.java     -- JML project nature
    LspCommandHandler.java                     -- Handles LSP command requests

Build requirements:
  ECLIPSE_HOME must point to an Eclipse installation that includes:
  LSP4E, LSP4J, TM4E, and standard Eclipse platform plugins.

To compile and package:
  bash build-update-site.sh --compile

To build the full update site artifact (plugin JAR + feature JAR + p2 metadata):
  bash build-update-site.sh

Output:
  bin/                               -- Compiled classes
  org.openjml.OpenJMLUI_<ver>.jar    -- Plugin JAR (copied to OpenJMLUpdateSite/plugins/)

The OpenJMLUpdateSite/ directory holds the p2 update site for distribution.
The OpenJMLGUITests/ directory holds SWTBot automated tests for this plugin.
